adder inflammation, which was positive in the patient's examination.", "LEU 18.000:Leu 18.000 refers to the elevated white blood cell count found in the patient's laboratory tests, indicating possible infection or inflammation.", "PCR:PCR, or C-reactive protein, is a significant marker of inflammation, as indicated by elevated levels in the patient's laboratory results. It is commonly measured through a blood test that assesses inflammation in the body and is frequently utilized to evaluate various health conditions.", "TROPNINA ALTA SENSIBILIDAD:Troponina alta sensibilidad is a cardiac marker that was tested to rule out myocardial infarction in the patient.", "GLUCEMIA 290 MG/DL:Glucemia 290 mg/dL indicates the patient's elevated blood sugar level at the time of admission.", "CIRUGÍA:El servicio de Cirugía es responsable de la atención y tratamiento del paciente, incluyendo la nutrición parenteral y la colocación de sonda para alimentación enteral.", "DIGESTIVO:El servicio de Digestivo es consultado para la colocación endoscópica de la sonda para alimentación enteral del paciente.", "RANSON:RANSON refers to a scoring system utilized to evaluate the severity of acute pancreatitis in patients. This system comprises a set of criteria that incorporates both clinical and laboratory findings, allowing healthcare professionals to assess the condition's seriousness effectively. The Ranson criteria are essential for guiding treatment decisions and predicting patient outcomes in cases of acute pancreatitis.", "APACHE II:APACHE II is a severity scoring system designed to evaluate the prognosis of critically ill patients, including those suffering from acute pancreatitis. This scoring system measures the severity of illness in patients, providing a quantitative assessment that helps in determining the risk of complications. Specifically, a score of 10 or higher on the APACHE II scale indicates an increased risk of adverse outcomes. The tool is widely utilized in clinical settings to guide treatment decisions and improve patient management for those in critical condition.", "SONDA DE ALIMENTACIÓN ENTERAL:La sonda de alimentación enteral es un dispositivo que se planea colocar para proporcionar nutrición al paciente de manera directa al yeyuno.", "OBESIDAD GRADO 1:", "NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL TOTAL (NPT):NPT es un tipo de nutrición administrada intravenosamente que el paciente ha estado recibiendo para mantener su estado nutricional.", "SONDA NASOENTERAL:La sonda nasoenteral es un dispositivo médico que se ha colocado en el paciente para proporcionar nutrición enteral."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}